P1 FINDINGS

1. R2 remains open because the server emits the forbidden nonzero identifier
   on its response to a malformed session-less request.

   Contract: docs/spec/SMP1.md:207-210 says every session-less frame carries
   identifier 0 and any nonzero value is PROTOCOL_FRAME_INVALID; lines 227-231
   also state that frame-level failures use the zero pre-session sentinel.

   Implementation: dispatch detects session=None/request_id!=0 only after the
   frame has decoded (server.rs:532-553). answer_batch then calls respond with
   the original frame.session and frame.request_id (server.rs:381-383), and
   respond constructs the response from those unchanged fields
   (server.rs:477-486). Thus the new test's malformed open with identifier 7
   receives a session-less response carrying identifier 7. ProtocolFrame's
   codec validation restricts identifier 0 only for Hello, not session-less
   Response/Event frames (lib.rs:1015-1023), so the invalid response encodes
   and decodes. The test at server_tests.rs:2552-2588 asserts only the failure
   body code and misses the response header contradiction.

   Required closure: classify this as a frame-level failure before dispatch,
   or explicitly normalize the failure response to session=None/request_id=0;
   make codec/contract scope agree and pin the response header.

2. R2's newly stated genesis replay rule contradicts the implemented and
   tested result.

   Contract: docs/spec/SMP1.md:211-214 says replaying a genesis write answers
   the owner failure (second genesis already initialized), while also saying
   the session-less path closes after a head exists.

   Implementation: the session-less genesis branch checks head_binding first
   and returns SESSION_BINDING_INVALID before workspace_create or
   exchange_import can run (server.rs:567-575). The existing headed
   workspace.create test pins SESSION_BINDING_INVALID, numeric 33007
   (server_tests.rs:1273-1287), not an owner already-initialized failure.

   Required closure: freeze one replay outcome and make prose, implementation,
   and tests agree for both workspace.create and exchange.import.

